<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The page a widget is drawn on.

    Set as an ImageView src and recoloured at runtime with setColorFilter, which
    is SRC_ATOP: it replaces the RGB outright and keeps only the source alpha.
    That is what lets one drawable serve all six palettes in both brightnesses
    on minSdk 21, where background tint lists (API 31) are not available.

    The authored colour is Emerald's light paper, so the widget picker's preview
    shows the app's default scheme rather than a white slab.

    The 20dp radius is larger than the app's own near-square panels on purpose:
    from Android 12 the launcher clips widgets to its own corner radius, and a
    3dp corner would simply be shaved off. The manuscript squareness is carried
    by the ruled frame inside instead — see widget_jadwal.xml.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">
    <solid android:color="#F7F2E6" />
    <corners android:radius="20dp" />
</shape>
